---
import { rankedInvestors, fmt, benchmarkReturns } from '../lib/performance.js';
interface Props {
  investor: (typeof rankedInvestors)[number];
}
const { investor: d } = Astro.props;
---

<div data-record-detail>
  <p>
    <b
      >{d.windows.filter((w) => w.gap > 0).length} of six rolling five-year windows
      ahead of SPY.</b
    > Annualized gaps, with windows ending each December:
  </p>
  <div class="rolling-windows">
    {
      d.windows.map((w) => (
        <span>
          <>
            <small>
              {w.start}–{w.end}
            </small>
            <b class={w.gap >= 0 ? 'up' : 'down'}>{fmt(w.gap, 2)} pp/yr</b>
          </>
        </span>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p>
    These windows overlap; they are not independent tests of skill. Figures are
    approximate. The frame always uses the full ten-year result.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Maximum drawdown: not yet verified.</b> Annual observations miss intra-year
    losses; a daily total-return series is required.
  </p>
  <p>{d.detail}</p>
  <p><b>Data basis.</b> {d.method}</p>
  <p>
    <a href={d.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >{d.sourceLabel} ↗</a
    >{
      d.dataSources.map((source) => (
        <>
          {' '}
          ·{' '}
          <a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            {source.label} ↗
          </a>
        </>
      ))
    }
  </p>
  <table class="annual-record">
    <caption>Calendar-year returns · USD</caption><thead
      ><tr
        ><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">{d.vehicle}</th><th
          scope="col">SPY ETF</th
        ></tr
      ></thead
    ><tbody
      >{
        d.returns.map((value, i) => (
          <tr>
            <>
              <th scope="row">{2016 + i}</th>
              <td>{fmt(value, 2)}%</td>
              <td>{fmt(benchmarkReturns[i], 2)}%</td>
            </>
          </tr>
        ))
      }</tbody>
  </table>
</div>
